---
source: crates/nb-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
notability notes — Find, open and manage notes in your library (incl. trash)

Usage: notability notes <command>

Commands:
  create     Create an empty, seeded note
  delete     Move to trash, or --permanent
  duplicate  Copy a note
  favorite   Star or unstar a note (--off)
  get        One note: metadata, pages, recordings, Learn status; --format md for markdown
  index      Build/refresh the local full-text index (cache only)
  layout     Switch paged / pageless
  list       List notes (filter by folder, type, favourites; sort; paginate)
  move       Move a note to a folder (or unfiled)
  rename     Rename a note
  search     Search titles, optionally typed/handwritten text
  trash      Deleted notes: list, restore, purge, empty

Global Options:
  --filter-output <keys>              Filter output by key paths (e.g. foo,bar.baz,a[0,3])
  --format <toon|json|yaml|md|jsonl>  Output format
  --full-output                       Show full output envelope
  --help                              Show help
  --llms, --llms-full                 Print LLM-readable manifest
  --schema                            Show JSON Schema for command
  --token-count                       Print token count of output (instead of output)
  --token-limit <n>                   Limit output to n tokens
  --token-offset <n>                  Skip first n tokens of output
